From 979e5c38ade396b3764a71f5596d60599b45e3b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: staccDOTsol <22843601+staccDOTsol@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 13:46:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the openzoo CLI current instead of freezing it at first
 boot

Patch 0045 made the openzoo bootstrap a strict one-shot:
try-omarchy-openzoo-bootstrap.service carried
ConditionPathExists=!/var/lib/try-omarchy/openzoo-bootstrapped and the script
exited 0 as soon as that stamp existed, so `npm install -g openzoo` ran exactly
once, on the first online boot, and openzoo-proxy.service then ran that same
build of /usr/bin/openzoo forever. A guest installed today gets openzoo 0.51.4 -
whose payment rail is broken; 0.51.5 fixes it - and never sees the fix, because
nothing in the image ever asks npm again.

The bootstrap now runs on every online boot and is idempotent:

- The unit loses its ConditionPathExists. After/Wants=network-online.target,
  Type=oneshot and TimeoutStartSec=15min are unchanged.
- The script still installs nodejs and npm through pacman only when they are
  missing, then runs `npm install -g --no-fund --no-audit openzoo@latest`, which
  upgrades when the registry has something newer and is a no-op otherwise.
- The npm call runs under `timeout 10m`, so a hung or unreachable registry
  cannot hold the boot open until systemd's own timeout kills the unit.
- Failure is fatal only when there is nothing to fall back to: with openzoo
  already installed the failure is logged and the boot continues on the version
  already on disk, so boots without network behave exactly as before; with no
  openzoo installed the script still exits non-zero and the unit retries next
  boot.
- The stamp is still written after a successful install - openzoo-proxy.service
  and the first-launch gate depend on the CLI being present - it just no longer
  suppresses the run.
- The final log line reports which version ended up installed.

The user-session proxy deliberately gets no restart mechanism. The bootstrap is
ordered on network-online.target in the system manager and finishes before the
graphical session starts the user manager's default.target, so a normal boot
already starts openzoo-proxy.service from the upgraded binary; the only window
is an upgrade landing under a session that is already running. Closing it would
mean the root oneshot reaching into every logged-in user's session manager to
restart the proxy, which can tear down an x402 request mid-payment to save one
reboot. Not trivial, not safe, left out.

The unit and the script are both in the compat overlay, so compat_revision goes
12 -> ... 13 -> 14: persistent disks created by earlier releases must receive
the rerunning unit, or exactly the machines this fixes would keep the frozen
one.

guest/tests/test_openzoo.py and guest/tests/verify.py pin the new contract: the
unit has no ConditionPathExists, the script asks for openzoo@latest under a
bounded timeout and no longer short-circuits on the stamp, and the compat
revision is 14.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nnYjoxQv7k7SoVmzzoKBr
